Jenkins SCM Polling Approach followed for the current setup


Developer
   ↓
git commit
   ↓
   git push
GitHub
        ↓
GitHub gets new commit
   ↓
Jenkins SCM Polling
   ↓
Jenkins detects new commit
   ↓
Reads Jenkinsfile from repo
   ↓
Maven Build
   ↓
Docker Build
   ↓
Trivy Security Gate
   ↓
Docker Push


-----------------------------------------------------------

git push
   ↓
GitHub
   ↓
Jenkins checks repository
   ↓
Detects new commit
   ↓
Build starts

Steps:


1. Keep Jenkinsfile in your GitHub repo

HospitalManagementSystem-Devops-Automation/
│
├── Jenkinsfile
├── HospitalManagement-Backend/
└── HospitalManagement-Frontend/

2. Jenkins → Configure → Pipeline

Use:

Definition: Pipeline script from SCM
SCM: Git
Repository:
https://github.com/tejaswini-arc/HospitalManagementSystem-Devops-Automation.git
Branch:
*/master
Script Path:
Jenkinsfile

3. Build Triggers

Select:

☑ Poll SCM

Set the schedule to:
H/5 * * * *
This means Jenkins checks GitHub approximately every 5 minutes.

For faster testing, you can temporarily use:
H/1 * * * *
which checks approximately every minute.

Important point about "Jenkinsfile every time"

You do not need to separately commit the Jenkinsfile every time.